{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1543754-implications-of-controlling-the-essence-flow-in-an-entire-city","id":1543754,"title":"Implications of controlling the Essence Flow in an entire city???","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-14T08:24:27-07:00","id":1543754,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Implications of controlling the Essence Flow in an entire city???","content":"<br /> I\u2019m reminded of a WtF NPC named Olivia Citysmith (WoD: Chicago 1st Ed) who was working to control the Essence Flow in the entire city and I have a player in my current Los Angeles chronicle that has an interest in attempting that feat. What could one be capable of by achieving this? How might local mages (Pentacle or Seer or Banisher) react if any became aware? How might spirits react? PROS? CONS? Who or what else might be inspired to take action in some manner?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T17:40:53-07:00","id":1543804,"title":"","content":"Being able to steer the tenor of spiritual activity in an area the size of a city could accomplish a wide variety of things depending on the city and its contents, namely by making certain areas more or less attractive or repulsive to certain kinds of spirits.<br /> <br /> Depending on how the project is being carried out and to what immediate consequences, local mages might be curious, apathetic, or irate \u2014 pinning the local ley lines with big un-veiled spells along Main Street to see how piscene Essence affects traffic is a different beast than quietly arranging for the road repairs in Little Italy to bury specially engraved tablets under the asphalt to quell passing vehicle-spirits, which is itself another matter apart from setting up pigeon coops on as many rooftops as you can get away with to propagate more avian qualities in the Shadow three stories and higher.<br /> <br /> Spirits are going to react the same way analogous animals would react from changes in their landscapes \u2014 the watering holes might move, predator populations might rise or fall and precipitate a counterpoint in the spirits they usually eat, some spirits might make a break for the Flesh in search of brighter pastures, and eventually a new equilibrium will form as long as more new variables don't get tossed in the pot.<br /> <br /> Anyone who can kind of spot what's going on, whether they realize it's a deliberate move or not, might take action if they have the influence to act against the methods or outcomes of the change and care for it sufficiently little.<br /> <br /> The pros are that this is basically the same type of large-scale Mystery tree-kicking as one gets from messing around with Nodes and Hallows.<br /> <br /> The cons are basically everything else that might happen. This kind of situation is a <i>gift</i> for the Long-Term Nimbus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T08:54:10-07:00","id":1543867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1543754-implications-of-controlling-the-essence-flow-in-an-entire-city?p=1543804#post1543804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone who can kind of spot what's going on, whether they realize it's a deliberate move or not, might take action if they have the influence to act against the methods or outcomes of the change and care for it sufficiently little.<br /> <br /> The pros are that this is basically the same type of large-scale Mystery tree-kicking as one gets from messing around with Nodes and Hallows.<br /> <br /> The cons are basically everything else that might happen. This kind of situation is a <i>gift</i> for the Long-Term Nimbus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, fascinating. Thanks, you\u2019ve got my gears turning! From my reading, it appears that a Node, Loci &amp; Dragons Nest are essentially the same thing so I could totally see a Mage or Dragon taking some measure of action to investigate any noteworthy occurrences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T00:26:07-07:00","id":1543958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DPowell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1543754-implications-of-controlling-the-essence-flow-in-an-entire-city?p=1543867#post1543867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, fascinating. Thanks, you\u2019ve got my gears turning! From my reading, it appears that a Node, Loci &amp; Dragons Nest are essentially the same thing so I could totally see a Mage or Dragon taking some measure of action to investigate any noteworthy occurrences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. Nodes are specific points along leylines. Loci are large collections of Essence, which I think often form at nodes but aren't necessarily tied to them. Dragon's Nests are just a generic term describing supernaturally interesting places. This could include both nodes and Loci (if a dragon actually recognizes them in the first place) but also places like &quot;an unidentified monster lives here&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}